1
00:00:01,055 --> 00:00:02,162
It's Christmas Day.

2
00:00:02,182 --> 00:00:04,704
Google says your favourite café is open.

3
00:00:04,809 --> 00:00:07,199
You drive there… and the door is locked.

4
00:00:07,651 --> 00:00:10,636
Busy owners forget to update their holiday hours.

5
00:00:10,656 --> 00:00:12,352
In Fonecta's challenge data,

6
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:17,060
almost half of all holiday listings will show the wrong hours this season.

7
00:00:18,021 --> 00:00:19,856
So we built Connect Suggests.

8
00:00:20,009 --> 00:00:22,914
Before every holiday, Connect checks every listing.

9
00:00:22,934 --> 00:00:26,527
When the hours will be wrong, the owner gets one short message,

10
00:00:26,547 --> 00:00:28,991
with the right hours and the reason why.

11
00:00:29,094 --> 00:00:29,550
One tap.

12
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:32,039
And it's live everywhere people search.

13
00:00:32,191 --> 00:00:33,268
Connect suggests.

14
00:00:33,288 --> 00:00:34,858
The customer approves.

15
00:00:36,315 --> 00:00:37,319
Let me show you.

16
00:00:37,339 --> 00:00:40,071
This is Kahvila Aurora, a café in Helsinki.

17
00:00:40,091 --> 00:00:44,593
Aleksi hasn't entered any holiday hours, so four days will be wrong.

18
00:00:44,845 --> 00:00:49,298
Connect works out the right hours from real clues: what he did last year,

19
00:00:49,318 --> 00:00:50,646
what similar cafés do.

20
00:00:50,666 --> 00:00:55,059
And one signal most people miss: on days a business was secretly closed,

21
00:00:55,079 --> 00:00:56,836
customer clicks drop by half.

22
00:00:56,856 --> 00:01:00,376
So we spot closures, even when the owner never told us.

23
00:01:00,628 --> 00:01:04,597
Aleksi gets one text, in his own language, at the time he prefers.

24
00:01:04,950 --> 00:01:06,107
No login. No app.

25
00:01:06,127 --> 00:01:10,675
This year he closes at 12 on Christmas Eve, so he just changes it.

26
00:01:10,695 --> 00:01:14,167
And he lets Connect handle holidays from now on.

27
00:01:14,319 --> 00:01:14,634
Done.

28
00:01:14,654 --> 00:01:19,056
The change goes through the Yext API that Connect already runs on,

29
00:01:19,076 --> 00:01:23,045
and Aleksi sees exactly where it goes live, and how fast.

30
00:01:23,297 --> 00:01:24,113
And it learns.

31
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:27,628
Next Christmas, his own answer comes back automatically.

32
00:01:27,941 --> 00:01:31,521
A brand-new customer with zero history? Connect still helps.

33
00:01:31,541 --> 00:01:34,811
And when it isn't sure, it asks instead of guessing.

34
00:01:34,912 --> 00:01:39,154
And if reviews say a business has closed for good, Connect sends nothing.

35
00:01:39,174 --> 00:01:40,609
A person checks first.

36
00:01:42,673 --> 00:01:46,585
Across all 3,000 Connect customers in the challenge data,

37
00:01:46,605 --> 00:01:50,204
that's 2,700 owners helped, with one message each.

38
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:53,683
Tested on businesses the model had never seen,

39
00:01:53,703 --> 00:01:56,300
it protects 69% of at-risk searches.

40
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,723
Copying last year protects 57%.

41
00:01:58,981 --> 00:02:03,572
For Fonecta, that means customers who see Connect working for them, and stay.

42
00:02:03,592 --> 00:02:07,814
And the same loop works for review replies, posts and opening hours.

43
00:02:08,071 --> 00:02:09,116
Connect suggests.

44
00:02:09,136 --> 00:02:10,494
The customer approves.

45
00:02:10,514 --> 00:02:13,170
And nobody walks to a closed door again.

